---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SpecCard from '../components/SpecCard.astro';
import { isHeld } from '../data/publish-queue.js';

const held = isHeld('/claudebot/');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="ClaudeBot: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It | PromptDNS"
  description="ClaudeBot explained: what Anthropic's crawler does, its user-agent token, robots.txt behavior, how to verify it, and how to block or allow it."
  breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["AI Web Infrastructure", "/ai-web-infrastructure/"], ["ClaudeBot"]]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">ClaudeBot</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">ClaudeBot: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">ClaudeBot is Anthropic's crawler that collects training data and retrieves pages for Claude. It honors robots.txt, and Disallow: ClaudeBot keeps it out. Genuine ClaudeBot fetches resolve to Anthropic-hosted addresses, which is how you verify them.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Crawler specification" data-vs="speccard-wrap">
      <SpecCard
        name="ClaudeBot"
        operator="Anthropic"
        token="ClaudeBot"
        purpose="training and retrieval for Claude"
        robots="honors Disallow: ClaudeBot"
        verify="Reverse DNS resolves to *.anthropic.com"
        evidence="Documented"
        verified="2026-10-28"
        href="/ai-crawlers-list/"
      />
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>How to block ClaudeBot</h2>
      <p>Add this rule to your robots.txt at the root of your domain:</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: ClaudeBot
Disallow: /</pre>
      <p>Anthropic documents separate tokens for user-initiated fetches (Claude-User) and search (Claude-SearchBot); blocking ClaudeBot only stops the training and retrieval crawler.</p>

      <h2>How to allow ClaudeBot</h2>
      <p>If you want ClaudeBot to crawl your site, make sure no rule disallows it. An explicit allow looks like this:</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: ClaudeBot
Allow: /</pre>
      <p>Then confirm from the live fetch with the <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">AI crawler checker</a>, which reads your published robots.txt the way a crawler would.</p>

      <h2>How to verify ClaudeBot</h2>
      <p>The reliable check is reverse DNS on the fetching IP address. Run the lookup below against any visitor claiming the ClaudeBot token; a genuine fetch resolves inside Anthropic's address space, and a spoofed one does not.</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">dig +short -x <fetching-ip>
# A genuine ClaudeBot fetch resolves to an Anthropic address</pre>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">Anthropic splitting crawl, user-fetch, and search into separate tokens is the most crawler-transparent behavior of the major AI vendors. It means you can allow Claude to answer questions about a page a user shared while still refusing training access, which is a policy most teams have not realized is possible.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I stop Claude from using my content for training?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Add User-agent: ClaudeBot with Disallow: / to robots.txt. Anthropic documents that ClaudeBot honors the rule.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is the difference between ClaudeBot and Claude-User?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">ClaudeBot crawls for training and retrieval. Claude-User fetches a page only when a Claude user asks about it directly. They are separate tokens with separate rules.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify a ClaudeBot visitor?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Reverse DNS on the fetching IP should resolve to an Anthropic address. If it does not, the visitor is spoofing the token.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Related:
        <a href="/ai-crawlers-list/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">all AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/how-to-block-ai-crawlers/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">how to block AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/how-to-allow-ai-crawlers/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">how to allow AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/robots-txt-guide/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">robots.txt guide</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
